// SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0
// specs/t27os/update_agent.t27 -- the running app serves its bundle and takes a friend's newer one (Refs gHashTag/t27#11560).
// Host side of update_view.t27. Two parts:
//   HELPER  the app's own executable started again with T27OS_UG_ROLE set (ug_main runs first in glass_window main and
//           never returns for a helper): ROLE=serve answers update requests on the listening socket the window made
//           (T27OS_UG_FD) with this bundle zipped (uh_zip_app) and a manifest signed by this device's identity, until the
//           window is gone; ROLE=fetch runs update_host.uh_update against the friend the window names and writes each
//           phase to its status file. Neither ever draws or touches the window's state.
//   WINDOW  ug_boot / ug_listen / ug_serve_start / ug_tick / ug_click: paths, the stale-lock sweep at launch, the port, the
//           helpers started and reaped, their status records read into the UPV_* bytes the panel draws.
// Test aids (off by default, not product behavior): T27OS_UPDATE_TARGET=<absolute .app path> installs into that copy
// instead of the running bundle (the running app is never replaced by a test); T27OS_UPDATE_AUTO=1 takes the first offer
// as a click on UPDATE would. Every state change logs one UPDATESTAT line to stderr; the lock sweep logs UPDATELOCK.
// Flat namespace: every name here starts with ug_ / UG_.
module T27osUpdateAgent;

